activity at your operation, both indoor and outdoor  Listed source to determine extreme weather conditions prohibit or limit outdoor play.   Instructions on how a parent may contact the local Licensing office, access the Texas Abuse and Neglect Hotline, and access the HHSC website;  Preventing and responding to abuse and neglect of children, including: (A) Required annual training for employees; (B) Methods for increasing employee and parent awareness of issues regarding child abuse and neglect, including warning signs that a child may be a victim of abuse or neglect and factors indicating a child is at risk for abuse or neglect; (C) Methods for increasing employee and parent awareness of prevention techniques for child abuse and neglect; (D) Strategies for coordination between the center and appropriate community organizations; and (E) Actions that the parent of a child who is a victim of abuse or neglect should take to obtain assistance and intervention, including procedures for reporting child abuse or neglect;   Information on vaccine-preventable diseases for employees, unless your center is in the home of the permit holder    The operation's open door policy contradicts the minimum stanard requirement and reqires that parent notify the director prior to arrival that they wish to enter the operation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026372849","violation_type_title":"Policies Comply with Rules (26 TAC §746.201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2409-a-9","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419","date":"2024-04-19","original_code":"746.2409(a)(9)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-08","finding":"Safety Requirements for Cribs - Documentation that Crib Meets Applicable Federal Rules: 3 cribs used in the infant room did not have documentation available to verify the date of manufacture.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026252003","violation_type_title":"Safety Requirements for Cribs - Documentation that Crib Meets Applicable Federal Rules (26 TAC §746.2409(a)(9))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-603-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419","date":"2024-04-19","original_code":"746.603(a)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-08","finding":"Children's Records Maintained: 6 children's records were reviewed and observed to be mssing the following documentation:    3 were missing completed emergency contact  2 were missing contact information for release persons  1 was missing the child's home address  1 did not have emergecy medical authorization.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026452809","violation_type_title":"Children's Records Maintained (26 TAC §746.603(a))","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3505-e","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419","date":"2024-04-19","original_code":"746.3505(e)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-08","finding":"Diapering Procedures - Sanitizing Diaper Changing Area: The diaper changing table was not sanitized following a diaper change.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026332595","violation_type_title":"Diapering Procedures - Sanitizing Diaper Changing Area (26 TAC §746.3505(e))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4503-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1364677-i20240419","date":"2024-04-19","original_code":"746.4503(b)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-08","finding":"Cots, Beds, Mats Labeled With Child's Name: Nap mats used are no